## UC definition sync: metric-view and UC Page references stay in step with Unity Catalog

Context:
A UC metric view was recognised at load time (object_kind, per-column
dimension/measure role, MEASURE() SQL) but then treated as a plain table: a
measure became a numeric attribute and its definition (expression, comment,
synonyms) was lost. OntoBricks had no link to UC Pages (business glossary).
The ontology now stores only a reference (`ontobricks:derivedFrom`,
`ontobricks:glossaryRef`) and re-reads the content from Unity Catalog at every
Knowledge Graph build and every metadata refresh. Sync never writes to UC.
References live in `ontology["definition_refs"]`, not on
`classes[].dataProperties`, because the entity editor rebuilds attribute dicts
from their names on every save.

Changes:
1. src/back/core/databricks/uc/MetricViewDefinition.py (new)
   - Parses the metric-view YAML (`SHOW CREATE TABLE` body or bare YAML) into
     per-column `role` / `expr` / `comment` / `synonyms` / `display_name`.
     Malformed YAML soft-fails to `{}` with a warning.
2. src/back/core/databricks/uc/UnityCatalog.py, src/back/core/databricks/DatabricksClient.py
   - `_parse_measure_names` now delegates to `MetricViewDefinition` (one
     parser instead of the regex). `_show_create_ddl` is shared by
     `_metric_measure_names` and the new `get_metric_view_definition`, which
     raises `InfrastructureError` when the view cannot be read.
3. src/back/core/databricks/uc/GlossaryConnector.py, NotAvailableGlossaryConnector.py (new)
   - Read-only glossary interface. databricks-sdk 0.82.0 has no Pages /
     glossary endpoint, so the only implementation reports the API as
     unavailable (info log); references keep their last value with a warning.
4. src/back/objects/mapping/MetricViewBindings.py (new)
   - Derives `derivedFrom` targets from entity mappings + metric-view
     metadata (case-insensitive columns, excluded attributes skipped). A view
     missing from the loaded metadata keeps its binding while the mapping
     still reads it. Mappings are never modified.
5. src/back/objects/ontology/definitions/ (new sub-package)
   - `DefinitionReferences`: reference store, manual glossary refs, reconcile
     (refresh derivedFrom, prune refs of deleted entities, mirror synced text
     onto referenced classes), adopt synced content from a snapshot, API view.
   - `DefinitionSyncService`: reads each referenced metric view once and the
     glossary terms, stores the per-source synced content, and returns a drift
     report (updated with before/after and added/removed synonyms, unchanged,
     warning with `target_missing` / `source_unavailable`; last value kept).
     A newly raised or cleared warning also counts as a change so the OWL
     picks up `ontobricks:definitionWarning`.
6. src/back/core/w3c/owl/OntologyDefinitionAnnotations.py (new), OntologyGenerator.py, src/back/objects/ontology/Owl.py
   - Declares `ontobricks:derivedFrom`, `glossaryRef`, `syncedAt`,
     `definitionSource`, `metricExpression`, `definitionWarning` as
     `owl:AnnotationProperty` once; for synced items replaces `rdfs:comment`
     / `skos:altLabel` with the UC values and adds `rdfs:seeAlso` for a URL
     page reference. `Owl.generate_session_owl` reconciles references before
     generating; `DomainSession.ensure_generated_content` uses it, so every
     mapping save (which invalidates the OWL) refreshes `derivedFrom`.
   - OntologyGenerator: base-URI normalisation, group annotation declarations
     and a redundant comment compacted to keep the frozen class size.
7. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinGraphBuild.py, _build_pipeline.py
   - The session build syncs definitions before the OWL is regenerated
     (credentials are now validated first). The build result carries
     `definition_sync` and the task message ends with
     "N definitions updated, M warnings". Two log templates joined on one
     line to keep the frozen class size.
8. src/back/objects/domain/TableMetadataRefresh.py (new), Domain.py, _metadata_tasks.py
   - Extract Class: the per-table refresh duplicated in
     `Domain.update_metadata_tables` and `run_metadata_update_task` moved to
     `TableMetadataRefresh.refresh`.
   - Sync refresh runs the definition sync on the session and returns
     `definition_sync`. The async task syncs on an ontology snapshot and
     returns `definition_sync` + `definition_refs`; `save_metadata_tables`
     adopts them on Apply (only for references with the same target; manual
     glossary refs are never created from the payload).
9. src/back/objects/ontology/Editor.py
   - `/ontology/class/update` accepts `glossary_ref` and
     `attribute_glossary_refs` (empty value clears; payload validated before
     any change) and re-applies synced UC text (read-only rule).
10. src/api/routers/internal/ontology.py, domain.py, src/front/static/domain/js/domain-metadata.js
    - New `GET /ontology/definitions`. `/domain/metadata/save` accepts
      `definition_refs`; the metadata refresh UI forwards it on Apply.
11. tests/units/definitions/ (new), tests/units/architecture/baseline.json, tests/units/front/test_metadata_guard_ui.py
    - Parser, bindings, sync service, OWL output, hooks, glossary API tests.
      Baseline tightened by the ratchet. The metadata-guard static test now
      expects the Apply body `{ tables, definition_refs }`.
12. docs/user-guide.md
    - New section "UC 정의 동기화 (Metric Views · Pages)".

Notes:
- `src/agents/` is unchanged: no eval delta needed. The Graph Chat schema
  digest lists names only (no comments / synonyms), so synced definitions do
  not reach the chat prompt yet; adding them is a prompt change that needs an
  eval run.
- Deferred: UI drift panel and glossary-ref field, a real UC Pages connector,
  Pages write-back, OWL import of the definition annotations, sync on the
  external v1 `/build`, and a chat tool for metric-view queries.
- PyYAML is a transitive runtime dependency (mlflow); no lockfile change.

